  docs/departures-widget-plan.md's Ticket 1 section assumed - so this fixture
  is instead built by hand from the official Trias_StopEvents.xsd /
  Trias_JourneySupport.xsd / Trias_LocationSupport.xsd / Trias_Common.xsd /
  Trias_ModesSupport.xsd schema files (also fetched live from
  github.com/VDVde/TRIAS), which fully and unambiguously specify this
  element structure.

  Four StopEventResult entries, covering every case TriasDepartureProvider's
  status-derivation logic branches on:
    1. on-time, WITH real-time confirmation (EstimatedTime == TimetabledTime)
    2. on-time, WITH NO real-time data at all (no EstimatedTime element)
    3. delayed by 3 minutes (EstimatedTime 3 minutes after TimetabledTime) -
       matches the design handoff's own "+3 Min" example.
    4. cancelled (Service/Cancelled = true)
-->
